+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## Current state
+
+The app shows a blank page in a browser because neither `index.html` nor `js/app.js` exist at the project root. The existing `todos.feature` and `world.js` already presuppose these files, so the suite fails at the Before hook.
+
+## This voyage's work
+
+Created `features/app-index.feature` — a plumbing spec that explicitly pins:
+- `index.html` must exist at the project root
+- It must load `js/app.js` via a script tag
+- It must contain the new-todo input, the main section, and the footer section from the template
+
+Updated `watchbill.json` with `watch1` naming the new scenario, shifting the existing watches to 2-10.
+
+## Next leg
+
+QM dispatches watch1. Crew builds `index.html` from `assets/app-template.index.html` and creates the `js/app.js` module. The scenario in `features/app-index.feature` is the binding prerequisite — watch1 must go green before the deeper watches are reachable.
+
+## Open
+
+- `RIGGING.md` is absent. The project needs a `focused` command, `specs` directory, and `implementation` directory mapped. Shipwright can derive it at first fitting.
+- Once `index.html` and `js/app.js` exist, the watch2-10 scenarios exercise runtime behaviour through happy-dom in world.js.
\ No newline at end of file
